Overriding the `dotnet/project/assembly_name` setting by feature is not supported. The resulting data folder still contains the name from the non-overridden feature, as you noticed. Changing the name of the folder is not enough, you'd also have to change the name of the DLLs and the contents of various JSON files that contain dependency information. But even then, Godot would still be unable to find the init function because of the assembly name.

The usual pattern for this is to reuse the same assembly. Then you can check the export features with the [`OS.HasFeature`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_os.html#class-os-method-has-feature) API:

```csharp
if (OS.HasFeature("DEDICATED_SERVER"))
{
    GD.Print("Running the server export.");
}
else
{
    GD.Print("Running the client export.");
}
```
